    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN output confirms the heap-use-after-free at `yr_re_ast_split_at_chaining_point` line 480 — exactly matching the crash signature from the bug report.\n\nThe input `rule test { strings: $a = /.{0,300}?foo/ condition: $a }` creates a regex where a non-greedy `.{0,300}?` is the first child of the CONCAT node. When `yr_re_ast_split_at_chaining_point` splits at that node, it sets `concat->children_head` to the RANGE_ANY node, then frees it via `yr_re_node_destroy(child)`. The second call to the split function then reads `child->greedy` from the freed node.",
